@@ -56,4 +56,6 @@
         [name]: Tool.make({
           description:
-            "Read a text file or supported image, page through a large UTF-8 text file by line offset, or list a directory page. Relative paths resolve from the current location; absolute paths inside it are accepted, while external absolute paths require external_directory approval.\n\nBy default, this tool returns up to 200 lines from the start of the file.\nText content is capped at 16 KiB per read; displayed lines are limited to 2000 characters.\nLine accounting scans at most 256 KiB beyond the returned page. If `<range total_exact=\"false\">` appears, `total` is a lower bound; otherwise it is exact.\nIf a result returns `<stub status=\"...\">`, use the already visible content in the current context instead of reading the same range again.\nFor source files, use `<range>`, `<more>`, and optional `<outline>` to choose targeted ranges. Do not page sequentially unless full-file comprehension is needed.",
+            // 保留精心打磨的成功后提示原话；这不是工具执行层的读取禁令。
+            "Read a text file or supported image, page through a large UTF-8 text file by line offset, or list a directory page. Relative paths resolve from the current location; absolute paths inside it are accepted, while external absolute paths require external_directory approval.\n\nBy default, this tool returns up to 200 lines from the start of the file.\nText content is capped at 16 KiB per read; displayed lines are limited to 2000 characters.\nLine accounting scans at most 256 KiB beyond the returned page. If `<range total_exact=\"false\">` appears, `total` is a lower bound; otherwise it is exact.\nIf a result returns `<stub status=\"...\">`, use the already visible content in the current context instead of reading the same range again.\nFor source files, use `<range>`, `<more>`, and optional `<outline>` to choose targeted ranges. Do not page sequentially unless full-file comprehension is needed." +
+            "\nAfter a successful edit, write, or apply_patch, skip re-reading the file to confirm—the tool errors if it didn't work.",
           input: Input,
